From f30d5bb7e35ee8159ba4433eb2c311d488f3def5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Substring <frog2wah@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:44:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] output-management: fail custom timings instead of
 approximating them

When the timings given with set_custom_timings couldn't be programmed,
on a backend other than DRM or if the mode couldn't be added, a custom
mode with the same size and refresh rate was set instead, leaving the
timings to the backend. Those can be out of range for the display, a
CRT monitor especially, and the client isn't told.

Fail the configuration instead, without passing it to the compositor,
and say so in the protocol.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
